us="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>APPLIED MATERIALS INC</name><address><country>US</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITO KAZUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI YOUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>APPLIED MATERIALS INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, KAZUYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI, YOUJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITO KAZUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI YOUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, KAZUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI, YOUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An epitaxial growth device (1) comprises a susceptor drive (7) for rotating a susceptor (6) in a process chamber (2). The susceptor drive (7) includes a support shaft (8) connected with the susceptor (6), a member (11) to be driven, and an annular member (13) located outside the member (11) and provided with a plurality of permanent magnets (12). The member (11) includes a magnetic material (11b) with an anticorrosive coating (H) that consists of a nickel layer (N), a chrome layer (C), and a metal oxide layer (O) formed by inactivation using ozone.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif de croissance épitaxiale (1) comprenant un dispositif d'entraînement (7) pour suscepteur, destiné à faire pivoter un suscepteur (6) à l'intérieur d'une chambre de traitement (2). Ce dispositif d'entraînement (7) pour suscepteur comprend un arbre support (8) connecté audit suscepteur (6), ainsi qu'un élément (11) destiné à être entraîné et un élément annulaire (13), lequel est placé à l'extérieur de cet élément destiné à être entraîné (11) et muni d'une pluralité d'aimants permanents (12). L'élément destiné à être entraîné (11) comporte un corps magnétique (11b) qui présente un revêtement anticorrosion (H), constitué d'une couche de nickel (N), d'une couche de chrome (C), et d'une couche d'oxyde métallique (O), ce revêtement étant formé par inactivation à l'aide d'ozone.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>